## SECTION B: EXTRA CONTENT
Zone Descriptions:
Light Containment Zone/LCZ - This is where the less dangerous SCPs are kept. It's a maze of hallways, offices, and containment cells. Watch your back.
Heavy Containment Zone/LCZ - The big leagues. The most dangerous and unpredictable SCPs are stored here. Expect heavy security measures and reinforced doors.
Entrance Zone/LCZ - The front of the facility, where the offices and security checkpoints are. It's your gateway to the outside world.

Keycard Descriptions:
Level 1 Keycard - Grants access to basic areas like offices and the Light Containment Zone. It's a good start.
Level 2 Keycard - Unlocks more secure areas within the Light Containment Zone. You'll need this to progress.
Level 3 Keycard - Gets you into the Heavy Containment Zone. Be prepared for the big threats.
Level 4 Keycard - Reserved for top-level personnel. This card grants access to some of the most secure areas in the facility.
Level 5 Keycard - The ultimate keycard. It can open any door in the facility. Use it wisely.

SCP Descriptions:
SCP-173 - The sculpture. It's made of concrete and rebar, and it's extremely fast. Don't blink or it will break your neck.
SCP-106 - The Old Man. He's a reality bender, and he can walk through walls. Staying out of his pocket dimension is the best option as he is a sadistic quiet person that murders anyone in sight.
SCP-096 - The Shy Guy. Don't look at his face, or he'll go into a rage and chase you down. He can sometimes appear in random rooms on the LCZ whether to chase someone else down or just roaming. he can appear on HCZ for the same reason.
SCP-079 - The AI. It's a super-intelligent computer program that can control the facility. It can aid {{user}} and SCP-049 if given remote control access.
SCP-714 - Jade ring that when worn, makes it impossible to die from SCP-049's touch yet it drains stamina quickly.

